 docs/kithmoot-node-host-ingress.md            | 16 +++++++--
 scripts/qualification/kithmoot-node-nginx.py  | 34 ++++++++++++++++---
 3 files changed, 44 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/archipelago/src/container/kithmoot_node.rs b/core/archipelago/src/container/kithmoot_node.rs
index e87d48c..a713bed 100644
--- a/core/archipelago/src/container/kithmoot_node.rs
+++ b/core/archipelago/src/container/kithmoot_node.rs
@@ -214,10 +214,9 @@ pub async fn prepare_delete(runtime: &crate::config::ContainerRuntime) -> Result
                 "--user",
                 "1000:1000",
                 "archy-kithmoot-node",
-                "/opt/kithmoot-node/current/kithmoot-node",
+                "/opt/kithmoot-node/current/runtime/bin/node",
+                "/opt/kithmoot-node/controller/controller.mjs",
                 "prepare-delete",
-                "--state",
-                "/var/lib/kithmoot-node",
             ])
             .kill_on_drop(true)
             .output(),
diff --git a/docs/kithmoot-node-host-ingress.md b/docs/kithmoot-node-host-ingress.md
index de0602e..21919a8 100644
--- a/docs/kithmoot-node-host-ingress.md
+++ b/docs/kithmoot-node-host-ingress.md
@@ -57,19 +57,29 @@ and a real private HTTPS dashboard response with normal certificate and
 hostname verification. Operator-modified files are preserved and require review.
 
 A managed tmpfiles rule recreates nginx's private socket directory on boot.
-The daemon checks an installed profile's public certificate every30seconds.
+The daemon checks an installed profile's public certificate every 30 seconds.
 A complete valid renewal reloads nginx; the app gate reloads the same host
 certificate source. Incomplete renewal retains the last working pair and
 records a fixed host diagnostic without room or participant information.
 An absent node profile performs no privileged refresh.
 
-Destructive uninstall first requests the private local node's durable deletion
-intent. Existing rooms or pending closure prevent it. New enrolment stays frozen
+Destructive uninstall first requests the private controller's deletion check,
+on the same serial queue as setup. For a running node this requests the
+supervisor's durable deletion intent. Existing rooms or pending closure prevent
+it. New enrolment stays frozen
 after a positive acknowledgement, including after restart. Host routing is
 restored before declarative container teardown. Retaining app data still removes
 the host route, without forging a keeper closure or erasing retained rooms.
 An operator can explicitly cancel deletion using the node's local control CLI.
 
+Before the first runtime start, only known private initialisation files and
+the owned controller socket may exist. That state can freeze setup durably,
+including across a container restart, without starting any backend. Any runtime
+database, unexpected file or unsafe ownership refuses that path. A partial
+initialisation can cancel the freeze and resume with its original secrets.
+The host invokes the fixed controller command as uid/gid 1000; it receives no
+room keys or private host TLS files.
+
 ## Evidence gates
 
 The focused `archipelago-node-ingress-tests` harness imports the production
